From 14c784ea0c54a28df5be8c42d8822c145c61514d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:26:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 89/95] opengles: enable gfxstream's ASTC and ETC2 emulation
 features

gfxstream decompresses ASTC and ETC2 textures with compute shaders when
the host GPU cannot sample them, which is the case for ASTC on desktop
GPUs. Until gfxstream bf62e4b7 ("Hide transfer only queues when ASTC
and ETC2 emulation enabled") FrameBuffer turned both emulations on
unconditionally. Since then they follow the VulkanAstcEmulation and
VulkanEtc2Emulation features, which the virtio-gpu frontend sets and
this file does not, so with that gfxstream both emulations are off and
a GPU without native ASTC cannot sample the guest's ASTC textures
(ModAVD/ModAVD#39).

Set both features, as virtio_gpu_gfxstream_renderer.cpp does, and list
them with the other gfxstream features in the log.

Test: 10 Star Rail and 10 Arknights cold boots log "ASTC LDR emulation
      mode: Gpu" and "enable ETC2 emulation: true"; without this change
      both are off and the guest sees no optimal tiling support for ASTC
      4x4 or ETC2 RGB8. A guest program that uploads both formats behind
      a synchronization2 barrier and reads them back gets every texel
      right (with gfxstream 9068c3aa and bf62e4b7).

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#39
---
 android/android-emu/android/opengles.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/android/android-emu/android/opengles.cpp b/android/android-emu/android/opengles.cpp
index 65ccdd166..c00468607 100644
--- a/android/android-emu/android/opengles.cpp
+++ b/android/android-emu/android/opengles.cpp
@@ -478,6 +478,16 @@ static int startOpenglesRendererImpl(
         }
     }
 
+    // gfxstream emulates ASTC and ETC2 with compute shaders when the host GPU
+    // lacks them, which desktop GPUs do for ASTC. Since gfxstream bf62e4b7 it
+    // only does so when these features are set, as the virtio-gpu frontend
+    // does (ModAVD#39).
+    gfxstreamFeatures.VulkanAstcEmulation.setEnabled(true);
+    gfxstreamFeatures.VulkanEtc2Emulation.setEnabled(true);
+    absl::StrAppend(&reportGfxstreamFeatures,
+                    gfxstreamFeatures.VulkanAstcEmulation.getName(), ", ",
+                    gfxstreamFeatures.VulkanEtc2Emulation.getName(), ", ");
+
     std::string maxGuestVulkan = "1.3";
     if (const char* env = getenv("ANDROID_EMU_VK_ENABLE_1_4")) {
         // Allow force-enabling with env variable for tests
